hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1319","Bundar told us, Yahya and Abu Asim told us, they said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tamim bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the pecking of a crow, the bed of wild animals, and a man to settle in The place or place as the camel settles it, meaning in the mosque."
